🚗 Car Logo Quiz App

A React Native mobile application built for a school assignment. The app presents users with car logos and lets them select the correct brand name using a custom Question component and the @react-native-picker/picker dropdown library.

🛠️ Features

Custom Components: Reusable Question component for layout consistency.

Dynamic Picker: Dropdown option selection for each quiz item using @react-native-picker/picker.

Score Calculation: Score evaluation using simple if-else condition checks.

Feedback Alerts: Results dialog displaying tailored feedback based on the user's total score.

Vector Icons: Header icon powered by @expo/vector-icons/MaterialCommunityIcons.

Scrollable Layout: Responsive view wrapped in ScrollView with full height padding.

📂 Project Structure

├── App.js                  # Main application container & logic
├── components/
│   └── question.js         # Custom re-usable question component
├── package.json            # Dependencies and app scripts
└── README.md               # Project documentation


🚀 Getting Started

1. Prerequisites

Ensure you have the following installed on your machine:

Node.js (v14 or higher recommended)

npm or yarn

Expo Go App (on your iOS/Android physical device) or Android Studio / Xcode Emulator

2. Installation

Install the required dependencies, including the React Native Picker and Vector Icons packages:

# Install general dependencies
npm install

# Install picker library
npm install @react-native-picker/picker

# Install Expo Vector Icons (if using Expo)
npx expo install @expo/vector-icons


🏃 Running the App

Start the Expo development server:

npx expo start


Android Emulator: Press a in your terminal window.

iOS Simulator: Press i in your terminal window.

Physical Device: Scan the QR code displayed in your terminal using the Expo Go app.

📝 Technologies Used

React Native (Functional Components, useState)

Expo Framework

@react-native-picker/picker

@expo/vector-icons